---
// Verbatim Authentic Content & Media from Khao Sok Riverside Cottages
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';

---

<PageLayout
  title="Rare and Endangered species of the Khao Sok national park"
  description="Discover the rare and endangered species of the Khao Sok national park in Thailand. We list endangered animals, birds and plants."
  heroImage="/wp-content/uploads/2019/04/pangolin-thailand.jpg"
  heroTitle="Rare and Endangered species of the Khao Sok national park"
  heroSubtitle="The Ancient Rainforest of Southern Thailand"
  breadcrumbs={[{"label": "Rare Endangered Species Khao...", "href": "/rare-endangered-species-khao-sok/"}]}
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-10">
    <div class="bg-[#faf8f5]/95 border border-[#12281b]/10 rounded-3xl p-4 sm:p-8 md:p-12 shadow-2xl backdrop-blur-md">
      
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-[#12281b]/10 pb-4 mb-8 font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.22em] uppercase text-[#163824]">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 font-semibold">
          <span class="text-[#7a5813]">KSR</span>
          <span class="text-[#12281b]/20">/</span>
          <span>FIELD DISPATCH</span>
        </div>
        <span class="text-[#7a5813] font-bold">KHAO SOK · THAILAND</span>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-6 text-[#223e2c] text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed font-normal">

        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <span>This area of Thailand that we now call Khao Sok has always been remote and inaccessible. The result, an incredible explosion of nature. Being so remote we find many unique and even endemic species. However, changes in the environment and the encroachment of people put many of these species at risk. This article lists some of the endangered animals and other rare and endangered species of the <a href="/khao-sok-national-park/" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">Khao Sok national park in Thailand</a>.</span>
        </p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>History of the area</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The dramatic limestone topography makes access to this area extremely difficulty. It is the fundamental reason why there is such a phenomenal number of unique or rare species here. In the 1970s, student activists set up a stronghold in the Khao Sok jungle. At this time commercial loggers and miners were plundering many of the more remote areas of Thailand. The activists kept them out of the forests of Khao Sok, further preserving the nature that lived here. The students were eventually pardoned and in 1980 the Khao Sok national park was formed.
        </p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Rajaprabha Dam & Cheow Lan Lake</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          This was closely followed by construction of the Rajaprabha Dam. It was seen as catastrophic for wildlife at the time. For example it is estimated that 52 species of fish were lost, mainly by the stagnation of the Pasaeng River as it morphed into the <a href="/cheow-lan-lake-information-guide/" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">Cheow Lan lake</a>. Despite this, the resultant landscape is now home to an extraordinary number and diversity of species. The Cheow Lan lake now provides access to the furthest reaches of the Khao Sok national park. It has become a natural playground that is high on the bucket lists of travellers to Thailand. An amazing number of people can now witness this incredible diversity.
        </p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Endangered Species – the pressure of human activity</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          Unfortunately there is a downside to all this human activity. Encroachment around the park damages the natural habitats that these endangered plants and animals depend on. Changes in climate and <a href="/khao-sok-weather/" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">weather patterns</a> put even more pressure on the wildlife of Khao Sok national park. Below we will attempt to list the endangered animals, birds, fish and plants that you might still be able to enjoy during your Khao Sok national <a href="/khao-sok-tours/" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors">park adventures</a>.
        </p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>The International Union for Conservation of Nature (IUCN)</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          The International Union for Conservation of Nature (IUCN) is the world’s oldest and largest global network of Environmental networks, combining over 1000 governments and NGOs (Non-Government Organisations) from over 160 countries. We use their categories as shown here:
        </p>
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Extinct</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <img decoding="async" class="lazyload alignleft wp-image-38116" src="https://www.khao-sok-riverside-cottages.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/extinct.png" data-orig-src="https://www.khao-sok-riverside-cottages.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/extinct.png" alt="Red list extinct" width="40" height="40" srcset="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%27http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%27%20width%3D%2740%27%20height%3D%2740%27%20viewBox%3D%270%200%2040%2040%27%3E%3Crect%20width%3D%2740%27%20height%3D%2740%27%20fill-opacity%3D%220%22%2F%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E" data-srcset="https://www.khao-sok-riverside-cottages.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/extinct-66x66.png 66w, https://www.khao-sok-riverside-cottages.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/extinct.png 123w" data-sizes="auto" data-orig-sizes="(max-width: 40px) 100vw, 40px" /><strong>Extinct</strong> – no reasonable doubt that the last individual has died
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <img decoding="async" class="lazyload alignleft wp-image-38119" src="https://www.khao-sok-riverside-cottages.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/extinct-wild.png" data-orig-src="https://www.khao-sok-riverside-cottages.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/extinct-wild.png" alt="Red list - extinct in the wild" width="40" height="40" srcset="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%27http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%27%20width%3D%2740%27%20height%3D%2740%27%20viewBox%3D%270%200%2040%2040%27%3E%3Crect%20width%3D%2740%27%20height%3D%2740%27%20fill-opacity%3D%220%22%2F%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E" data-srcset="https://www.khao-sok-riverside-cottages.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/extinct-wild-66x66.png 66w, https://www.khao-sok-riverside-cottages.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/extinct-wild.png 123w" data-sizes="auto" data-orig-sizes="(max-width: 40px) 100vw, 40px" /><strong>Extinct in the Wild</strong> – only surviving in captivity
        </p>
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Threatened</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <a href="/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/critically-endangered.png" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors"><img decoding="async" class="lazyload alignleft wp-image-38125" src="https://www.khao-sok-riverside-cottages.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/critically-endangered.png" data-orig-src="https://www.khao-sok-riverside-cottages.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/critically-endangered.png" alt="Red list - Critically Endangered species" width="40" height="40" srcset="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%27http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%27%20width%3D%2740%27%20height%3D%2740%27%20viewBox%3D%270%200%2040%2040%27%3E%3Crect%20width%3D%2740%27%20height%3D%2740%27%20fill-opacity%3D%220%22%2F%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E" data-srcset="https://www.khao-sok-riverside-cottages.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/critically-endangered-66x66.png 66w, https://www.khao-sok-riverside-cottages.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/critically-endangered.png 123w" data-sizes="auto" data-orig-sizes="(max-width: 40px) 100vw, 40px" /></a><strong>Critically Endangered</strong> – facing an extremely high risk of extinction in the wild
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <img decoding="async" class="lazyload alignleft wp-image-38126" src="https://www.khao-sok-riverside-cottages.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/endangered.png" data-orig-src="https://www.khao-sok-riverside-cottages.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/endangered.png" alt="Red list endangered animals" width="40" height="40" srcset="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%27http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%27%20width%3D%2740%27%20height%3D%2740%27%20viewBox%3D%270%200%2040%2040%27%3E%3Crect%20width%3D%2740%27%20height%3D%2740%27%20fill-opacity%3D%220%22%2F%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E" data-srcset="https://www.khao-sok-riverside-cottages.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/endangered-66x66.png 66w, https://www.khao-sok-riverside-cottages.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/endangered.png 123w" data-sizes="auto" data-orig-sizes="(max-width: 40px) 100vw, 40px" /><strong>Endangered</strong> – facing a very high risk of extinction in the wild
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <a href="/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/vulnerable.png" class="text-[#1b432c] underline decoration-[#ba9038]/60 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#ba9038] hover:text-[#7a5813] transition-colors"><img decoding="async" class="lazyload alignleft wp-image-38127" src="https://www.khao-sok-riverside-cottages.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/vulnerable.png" data-orig-src="https://www.khao-sok-riverside-cottages.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/vulnerable.png" alt="Red list vulnerable species" width="40" height="40" srcset="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%27http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%27%20width%3D%2740%27%20height%3D%2740%27%20viewBox%3D%270%200%2040%2040%27%3E%3Crect%20width%3D%2740%27%20height%3D%2740%27%20fill-opacity%3D%220%22%2F%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E" data-srcset="https://www.khao-sok-riverside-cottages.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/vulnerable-66x66.png 66w, https://www.khao-sok-riverside-cottages.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/vulnerable.png 123w" data-sizes="auto" data-orig-sizes="(max-width: 40px) 100vw, 40px" /></a><strong>Vulnerable</strong> – facing a high risk of extinction in the wild
        </p>
        <h3 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Least Concern</span>
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <img decoding="async" class="lazyload alignleft wp-image-38130" src="https://www.khao-sok-riverside-cottages.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/near-threatened.png" data-orig-src="https://www.khao-sok-riverside-cottages.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/near-threatened.png" alt="Red list - near threatened" width="40" height="40" srcset="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%27http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%27%20width%3D%2740%27%20height%3D%2740%27%20viewBox%3D%270%200%2040%2040%27%3E%3Crect%20width%3D%2740%27%20height%3D%2740%27%20fill-opacity%3D%220%22%2F%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E" data-srcset="https://www.khao-sok-riverside-cottages.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/near-threatened-66x66.png 66w, https://www.khao-sok-riverside-cottages.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/near-threatened.png 123w" data-sizes="auto" data-orig-sizes="(max-width: 40px) 100vw, 40px" /><strong>Near Threatened</strong> – close to or is likely to qualify for a threatened category
        </p>
        <p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-[#223e2c]">
          <img decoding="async" class="lazyload alignleft wp-image-38131" src="https://www.khao-sok-riverside-cottages.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/least-concern.png" data-orig-src="https://www.khao-sok-riverside-cottages.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/least-concern.png" alt="Least Concern" width="40" height="40" srcset="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%27http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%27%20width%3D%2740%27%20height%3D%2740%27%20viewBox%3D%270%200%2040%2040%27%3E%3Crect%20width%3D%2740%27%20height%3D%2740%27%20fill-opacity%3D%220%22%2F%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E" data-srcset="https://www.khao-sok-riverside-cottages.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/least-concern-66x66.png 66w, https://www.khao-sok-riverside-cottages.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/least-concern.png 123w" data-sizes="auto" data-orig-sizes="(max-width: 40px) 100vw, 40px" /><strong>Least Concern</strong> – widespread and abundant
        </p>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-[#163824] font-semibold tracking-tight mt-10 mb-4 pt-6 border-t border-[#12281b]/10">
          <span>Endangered Animals of Khao Sok national park</span>
        </h2>
